    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `membershipNumber` as a derived, read-only field `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`).\n\n**Two small, cohesive changes** \u2014 no new class, no Owner model field, no DB column, no pipeline step:\n\n1. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one `@Mapping` expression on the existing `toOwnerDto` method, mirroring how `displayName`/`initials` are already derived. It reads the owner's own `customerCode` and `registrationDate`, formatting `YY` as the last two digits of the registration year (`year % 100`, zero-padded), guarding nulls.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipNumber` read-only property to the `Owner` schema so the generated DTO has the field.\n\nBecause it's derived at mapping time from persisted fields, it appears identically on both POST-create and GET responses and is seed-independent, exactly as the test (`createOwnerOk` \u2192 `fetchOwner`) requires.\n\nStructural impact was kept minimal: I touched 2 files and modified a single abstract mapper method (CC 1, negligible surrounding WMC) plus a schema addition \u2014 no growth of any existing method or class.",
